# Game design (SpecialPG)

Read [docs/game/vision.md](../../docs/game/vision.md) and the matching section of [docs/game/scope-and-phases.md](../../docs/game/scope-and-phases.md).

## Precedence

| Question | Wins |
|----------|------|
| Coordinates, saves, map integrity | [architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md) |
| Should this feature exist **now**? | [scope-and-phases.md](../../docs/game/scope-and-phases.md) |
| Setting tone and factions | [vision.md](../../docs/game/vision.md) |

## Rules

- **Phase 0–1** is the default implementation window unless the task names a higher phase.
- Do not paste Palladium PDF rule text into the repo — use [rifts-source-index.md](../../docs/game/rifts-source-index.md) (`RIFTS_SOURCE_ROOT`).
- Faction/region **labels** in data are OK; full stat blocks and combat math are Phase 5+.
- Shell/terrain bugfixes do not require game vision unless they change player-facing meaning.

See also [agent-pitfalls.md](../../docs/agent-pitfalls.md) § Scope creep.
